From 49a966a8e347ff250d1e10b8385109a1c01fb9be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:38:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [GBM] Switch refresh rates seamlessly with variable refresh
 rate

A display driven with variable refresh rate (FreeSync) switches between
modes that only differ in their vertical front porch without
resynchronising, so changing the refresh rate for playback no longer
blanks the picture. The kernel reports such a connector as vrr_capable
and, on the Raspberry Pi, adds those modes for the common video rates.

When the connector is vrr_capable, set VRR_ENABLED on the CRTC with the
mode, flag the modes that have such a sibling with D3DPRESENTFLAG_VRR,
and let the refresh rate matcher prefer a flagged mode of a whitelisted
size at the frame rate or twice it before the standard search.

Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
